title: where a save's warnings go
pid: 7de55650-4078-47a4-9689-d8007fdbf22b
body: |2-
  A save's own warnings and errors go to a buffer of their own,
  replaced at each save that has any: =*SKG Save Warnings*=,
  =*SKG Save Errors - Inconsistencies Found*= when the save was
  refused, or =*SKG Save Errors and Warnings*= when it has both. One
  such warning names each orphan graphnode the save created: a node
  that no list contains, made from a headline typed under a parent
  that reads no claims ('docs/glossary.org', "claims membership",
  lists those parents). A new view root is in no list either, but is
  not warned of.

  A rerender that follows a command (C-c v l, 'skg-restrict-repo-set';
  a commit; an import; the
  cleanup of references to an absent node, the extension of the diff
  view, or M-x skg-request-rerender-all-views) has errors and
  warnings of its own, which go to =*skg rerender messages*=.
